  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Greetng By Billy**: rare: 4 archived performances [2]\n- **Turmoil And Tnfoil**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Randall Collins**: back after 155 archived shows (980 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **Done Gone**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **Kissimmee Kid**: back after 108 archived shows (751 days); rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Cabin Home**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **Band Introdctions**: rare: 4 archived performances [2]\n- **Nutshell**: rare: 9 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2025-04-05** (recommended): source not stated; 26 songs; 165 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Notes label this recording show number 81 of 2025 for the taper, released by A Team Dirty South and Home Team Recording [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2025-04-05**: taped by Z-Man; transferred by Z-Man; source: Schoeps CCM4V'S>Sound Devices Mix-Pre 6 II (48/32) [1]. Also: Recorded by Z-Man with Schoeps CCM4V microphones into a Sound Devices Mix-Pre 6 II at 48kHz/32-bit, with Micah Ennis assisting; Taped from Section 102, Row A, Seat 117, with the microphones held 6.5 feet high; processed via Sound Forge, CD Wave, then FLAC 16-bit [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings St. Augustine Amphitheatre - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/venue/the-st-augustine-amphitheatre/) [3]\n- Fan art by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings St. Augustine N2 - Regular Poster - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/merch/st-augustine-n2-regular-poster/) [4]\n- Poster by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings St. Augustine 2025 Run - Regular Poster - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/merch/st-augustine-2025-run-regular-poster/) [5]\n- Poster by panetory.com: [Billy Strings St. Augustine Amphitheatre Apr 5 2025 Poster 2026](https://panetory.com/billy-strings-st-augustine-amphitheatre-apr-5-2025-poster) [6]",
